From d99c0d2d690d97523a0ea41e8781a72cf5a77c43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wiesion <wiesion@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:26:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] [XPU][Attention] INT8 per-token-head KV cache for paged
 decode

Add vLLM's int8_per_token_head KV cache dtype to the Xe2 paged decode
(split-K) FlashAttention path.

- KV dtype int8 with one fp32 scale per (KV token, KV head). The scales are
  passed through the existing k_descale / v_descale arguments as strided
  scale caches [num_blocks, block_size, num_heads_kv]; no op schema change.
- Layout: per block [int8 K|V for all (slot, head) | K scales | V scales]
  (same bytes per block as vLLM's inline per-token-head layout, arranged so
  every K/V base is 64-byte aligned for Xe 2D block loads). Because the block
  stride is not a whole number of KV tiles, INT8 tiles are loaded through
  per-block 2D surfaces.
- Dedicated INT8 tile step in DecodeFwdMainloop: one page-table read per
  tile, scale loads issued before the K loads, K scale applied to the S
  columns before masking, V scale to the P columns after the softmax row
  sums. Tokens at or beyond seq_len get scale 0. fp16/bf16/fp8 paths are
  unchanged.
- flash_api: validate the INT8 cache/scale views; INT8 KV is paged decode
  only (max_seqlen_q == 1, plus the uniform small-q speculative-decode route
  that runs through the decode kernel). Prefill callers dequantize the
  referenced blocks and use the fp16/bf16 kernel.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
Signed-off-by: Thomas Wieser <thomas@wiesion.ch>

Adapted from: https://github.com/wiesion/vllm-xpu-kernels/commit/60668c49a156f85ef397ac54c4759fc45f4b2f78
  (branch int8-kv-llmscaler, intel/llm-scaler#744 / #739; Apache-2.0, DCO
  signed off by the author). Port onto vllm-xpu-kernels 0.1.16.2 (6b30c9b +
  b70.5): CutlassDType moved to csrc/xpu/attn/fmha_utils.hpp; the KV head is
  passed to both has_large_surface instantiations of the decode mainloop, and
  INT8 KV never takes the 2^24-row surface split (it builds one surface per
  KV block); q_descale normalisation kept; fp8 Q with INT8 KV rejected.
Ported-by: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>

